{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And HaShem relented and was grieved to His heart.</b> The Torah spoke in the language of human beings. The meaning is that they rebelled and grieved His holy spirit with their transgressions. And the meaning of \"to His heart\" is that He did not declare this to a prophet sent to them; and likewise the expression denotes what is in thought, in the manner of \"to speak to my heart\" (Genesis 24:45) and similar verses. And in Bereshit Rabbah (Genesis Rabbah 27:4) the Sages said concerning this a weighty matter by way of a parable that they brought from the broker and the steward, and it is a great mystery not permitted to be written, and the one who knows it will contemplate why here the particular Name is stated whereas in the entire passage and the matter of the Flood the name Elohim is used."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:20:37.099421981Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}